# React Router 7 Type Safety

v7 generates per-route type namespaces. Each route file has a sibling `./+types/<file-base>` import that resolves to a generated `.react-router/types/...` file. The generated file declares a `Route` namespace with `LoaderArgs`, `ActionArgs`, `MetaArgs`, `HeadersArgs`, `ComponentProps`, `ErrorBoundaryProps`, `LinksFunction`, and `ShouldRevalidateFunctionArgs`. URL params and Single Fetch serialization shapes are typed end-to-end.

## tsconfig.json

```json
{
  "include": ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", ".react-router/types/**/*"],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["DOM", "DOM.Iterable", "ES2022"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "strict": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "rootDirs": [".", "./.react-router/types"],
    "types": ["@react-router/node/globals", "vite/client"],
    "paths": { "~/*": ["./app/*"] }
  }
}
```

The two load-bearing keys are `include` (must contain `.react-router/types/**/*`) and `rootDirs` (lets `./+types/<name>` resolve to a sibling-virtual path).

## package.json scripts

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "react-router dev",
    "build": "react-router build",
    "start": "react-router-serve ./build/server/index.js",
    "typecheck": "react-router typegen && tsc"
  }
}
```

`react-router typegen` writes the types. `react-router dev` and `react-router build` run typegen as a side effect, but `tsc` does not, so wrap it.

## .gitignore

```
.react-router/
```

Generated types are deterministic and should not be checked in.

## Per-route usage

```tsx
// app/routes/products.$pid.tsx
import type { Route } from "./+types/products.$pid";

export async function loader({ params, request }: Route.LoaderArgs) {
  //  params.pid is string (typed from the file name)
  //  request is Request
}

export default function Product({ loaderData, actionData, params }: Route.ComponentProps) {
  // loaderData is the awaited return type of loader, after Single Fetch serialization
}
```

## Refused patterns

- `import type { LoaderFunctionArgs, LoaderFunction, ActionFunction, MetaFunction, LinksFunction } from "react-router"` for Framework Mode routes. These exist for Data Mode interop but lose typegen benefits.
- `useLoaderData<typeof loader>()`: bypasses Single Fetch typing. Use `Route.ComponentProps`.
- Bare `tsc` in CI without `react-router typegen` first: `Route` namespace types will be `any`.

Source: https://reactrouter.com/explanation/type-safety
